 ## 8\. Comic Panel Design

 The panel editor is the central part of ComicCraft.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Page 1                             │
├───────────────────┬────────────────┤
│                   │                │
│     PANEL 1       │    PANEL 2     │
│                   │                │
│  Alex enters      │ Finds robot    │
│  laboratory       │                │
│                   │                │
├───────────────────┴────────────────┤
│                                    │
│             PANEL 3                │
│                                    │
│       Robot suddenly awakens       │
│                                    │
└────────────────────────────────────┘
```

 Users should be able to:

 - Rearrange panels
- Edit descriptions
- Edit dialogue
- Change panel size
- Regenerate a panel
- Add/remove panels

 ## 9\. Dialogue Design

 Dialogue should be associated with individual panels.

 Example:

 **Panel 3**

 **Alex:**

 > "You're... actually alive?"

 **Robot:**

 > "System reboot complete."

 The user can request modifications such as:

 > "Make the dialogue funnier."

 or

 > "Make the conversation more dramatic."

 ## 10\. AI Interaction Design

 Rather than giving users one large AI-generated result, ComicCraft should use smaller AI operations.

```
User Idea
   ↓
Gemini
   ↓
Story Structure
   ↓
Gemini
   ↓
Characters
   ↓
Gemini
   ↓
Scenes
   ↓
Gemini
   ↓
Panels + Dialogue
```

 This makes individual results easier to review and regenerate.

